      <activity id="7360f1b2-03c0-506d-ba1f-24a872da72b8" activityNameId="0f37bd8a-fe32-5756-b269-a481b233d0cd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hydrogen, cracking, APME, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hydrogen, cracking, APME, at plant
Data are from the Eco-profiles of the European plastics industry (PlasticsEurope). Not included are the values reported for: recyclable wastes, amount of air / N2 / O2 consumed, unspecified metal emission to air and to water, mercaptan emission to air, unspecified CFC/HCFC emission to air, dioxin to water. The amount of "sulphur (bonded)" is assumed to be included into the amount of raw oil.;
CAS number: 001333-74-0; 
UUID: 5ac0612d-cd34-3b83-bfc8-a9bf1983b68b
Aggregated data for all processes from raw material extraction until delivery at plant
Location: 17 European plants
Technology: production during cracking of naphtha
Time period: time to which data refer
Production volume: worldwide 240 billion m3 in 1988
Sampling: literature values based on company survey 
Extrapolations: no extrapolation
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5ac0612d-cd34-3b83-bfc8-a9bf1983b68b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
